Probability -- basic probability functions
******************************************

Description
===========

This package provides a number of basic probability functions.  In particular,
for both discrete and continuous probability distributions, there are the
following four functions:

  * *note density: density,:  probability density (or mass) function
  * *note probability: probability,:  cumulative distribution function
  * *note quantile: quantile,:  quantile function
  * *note random(ProbabilityDistribution):
    random_lpProbabilityDistribution_rp,:  generate random samples

A variety of common probability distributions are supported.

Discrete distributions
----------------------

  * *note binomial: binomialDistribution,
  * *note Poisson: poissonDistribution,
  * *note geometric: geometricDistribution,
  * *note negative binomial: negativeBinomialDistribution,
  * *note hypergeometric: hypergeometricDistribution,

Continuous distributions
------------------------

  * *note uniform: uniformDistribution,
  * *note exponential: exponentialDistribution,
  * *note normal: normalDistribution,
  * *note gamma: gammaDistribution,
  * *note chi-squared: chiSquaredDistribution,
  * *note Student's t: tDistribution,
  * *note F: fDistribution,
  * *note beta: betaDistribution,

You may also define your own probability distributions using *note
discreteProbabilityDistribution: discreteProbabilityDistribution, and *note
continuousProbabilityDistribution: continuousProbabilityDistribution,.

Caveat
======

As is always the case when working with real numbers in Macaulay2, unexpected
results may occur due to the limitations of floating point arithmetic.

* Menu:

* ProbabilityDistribution::     probability distribution class

