ProbabilityDistribution -- probability distribution class
*********************************************************

Description
===========

This is the class of which all probability distribution objects belong.
ProbabilityDistribution is an abstract class defining the interface and should
not be used directly. Instead, its subclasses DiscreteProbabilityDistribution
and ContinuousProbabilityDistribution should be used.

ProbabilityDistribution objects are hash tables containing six key-value pairs:

DensityFunction
    The probability mass or density function (for discrete or continuous distributions, respectively).  Do not use this directly.  Instead, use *note density: density,.
DistributionFunction
    The cumulative distribution function.  Do not use this directly.  Instead, use *note probability: probability,.
QuantileFunction
    The quantile function.  Do not use this directly.  Instead, use *note quantile: quantile,.
RandomGeneration
    A function to generate random samples of the distribution.  Do not use this directly.  Instead, use *note random(ProbabilityDistribution): random_lpProbabilityDistribution_rp,.
Support
    A sequence of two numbers, the lower and upper bound of the support of the distribution.
Description
    A string containing a description of the distribution.  This is the return value when a ProbabilityDistribution object is passed to *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)net,.
