density -- probability density (or mass) function
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        density_X x
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note probability distribution: ProbabilityDistribution,, 
      * x, a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, 

Description
===========

For a discrete probability distribution, this returns values of of the
probability mass function (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/probability_mass_function ) of the distribution,
i.e., \(f_X(x) = P(X = x)\).

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = binomialDistribution(5, 0.25)|
|                                      |
|o1 = B(5,.25)                         |
|                                      |
|o1 : DiscreteProbabilityDistribution  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : density_X 2                      |
|                                      |
|o2 = .263671875                       |
|                                      |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : binomial(5, 2) * 0.25^2 * 0.75^3 |
|                                      |
|o3 = .263671875                       |
|                                      |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+

For a continuous probability distribution, this returns values of the
probability density function (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/probability_density_function ) of the
distribution, i.e., the integrand in \(\int_a^b f_X(x)\,dx = P(a\leq X \leq
b)\).

+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : Z = normalDistribution()         |
|                                      |
|o4 = N(0,1)                           |
|                                      |
|o4 : ContinuousProbabilityDistribution|
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : density_Z 0                      |
|                                      |
|o5 = .3989422804014327                |
|                                      |
|o5 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : 1/sqrt(2 * pi)                   |
|                                      |
|o6 = .3989422804014327                |
|                                      |
|o6 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : integrate(density_Z, -1, 1)      |
|                                      |
|o7 = .682689492137086                 |
|                                      |
|o7 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : integrate(density_Z, -2, 2)      |
|                                      |
|o8 = .9544997361034697                |
|                                      |
|o8 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i9 : integrate(density_Z, -3, 3)      |
|                                      |
|o9 = .997300204130616                 |
|                                      |
|o9 : RR (of precision 53)             |
+--------------------------------------+

Ways to use density:
====================

  * "density(DiscreteProbabilityDistribution,Number)"
  * "density(ProbabilityDistribution,Number)"

