random(ProbabilityDistribution) -- randomly generate samples from probability distribution
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note random: (Macaulay2Doc)random,
  * Usage: 
        random X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note probability distribution: ProbabilityDistribution,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Density: (Macaulay2Doc)random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, => ...,
        default value 1,
      * *note Height: (Macaulay2Doc)random_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, => ..., default
        value 10,
      * *note MaximalRank: (Macaulay2Doc)random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, => ...,
        default value false,
      * *note UpperTriangular: (Macaulay2Doc)random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, =>
        ..., default value false,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, 

Description
===========

Randomly generate samples from the given probability distribution.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Z = normalDistribution()                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = N(0,1)                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : ContinuousProbabilityDistribution                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
