geometricDistribution -- geometric distribution
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        geometricDistribution p
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, between 0 and 1; 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note discrete probability distribution: ProbabilityDistribution,, 

Description
===========

The geometric distribution (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/geometric_distribution ), the distribution of the
number of a failures in a sequence of Bernoulli trials before the first
success, where p is the probability of a success.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = geometricDistribution 0.1  |
|                                    |
|o1 = Geo(.1)                        |
|                                    |
|o1 : DiscreteProbabilityDistribution|
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : density_X 2                    |
|                                    |
|o2 = .08100000000000002             |
|                                    |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)           |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : probability_X 3                |
|                                    |
|o3 = .3439                          |
|                                    |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)           |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : quantile_X 0.4                 |
|                                    |
|o4 = 4                              |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : random X                       |
|                                    |
|o5 = 21                             |
+------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Some probability texts define the geometric distribution as the number of
Bernoulli trials until the first success, and so the values will be one greater
than ours.  Our definition is consistent with R.

